If You Need Files Larger Than 100 MB

Use Git LFS (Large File Storage):

Install:

Shell
sudo apt install git-lfs

Initialize:

Shell
git lfs install

Track files:

Shell
git lfs track "*.bin"
git lfs track "*.safetensors"
git lfs track "*.gguf"

Commit:

Shell
git add .gitattributes
git commit -m "Enable Git LFS"

Commonly used for:

Plain Text
Llama models
LoRA adapters
ML datasets
Model checkpoints
For Your AI SRE Project

The GitHub repository should mainly contain:

Plain Text
Dockerfile
requirements.txt
main.py
agents/
memory/
workflows/
k8s/
helm-chart/
README.md
.gitignore

Ideal repository size:

Plain Text
10 MB - 100 MB

For ArgoCD, you only need the source code and Kubernetes/Helm manifests, not virtual environments, Minikube binaries, or downloaded AI models.

Check What Is Making Your Repo Large

Run:

Shell
du -h --max-depth=1 | sort -hr

and

Shell
find . -type f -size +50M

Those two commands will immediately show which files/folders are causing the large push size.
